&lt;h2&gt;Opportunity &amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brunswick Group is seeking an enthusiastic and analytical Apprentice BI Data Analyst to join its Group Business Intelligence (BI) team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Group BI team plays a key role in supporting the business globally by delivering meaningful data, reporting and analysis to inform strategic decisions. Working closely with Finance, FP&amp;amp;A, the Commercial Hub and other business teams, the function develops and maintains reporting systems and BI dashboards, helping stakeholders better understand financial performance, revenue and recovery data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will work within the BI development team, reporting to the BI Technical Support Analyst. The role involves providing technical support, investigating and resolving reporting issues, and assisting with the development and improvement of dashboards to enhance self-service reporting across the firm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alongside gaining hands-on experience with Microsoft Dynamics 365, Azure SQL Server and Power BI, the successful candidate will complete a Level 4 Data Analyst Apprenticeship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a motivated individual with strong analytical and interpersonal skills, a keen interest in data and technology, and a willingness to learn. Previous Business Intelligence experience is not required, as training and mentoring will be provided. Applicants must meet the apprenticeship eligibility requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your day-to-day responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform daily integrity checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigating issues raised by end-users and resolve them or escalating them to the development team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide immediate solutions to system issues and liaise with other support teams to ensure prompt resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage small scale changes through to completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform quality assurance tests and assisting with new release processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate and enhance workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and administer reporting security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with people across the firm to enable them to self-serve Business Intelligence through Power BI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with developers to support the technical implementation and roll-out of new reporting dashboards on Power BI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As skills and knowledge are gained, personally take on development work, through SQL and Power BI within the team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Brunswick, we seek smart and curious individuals dedicated to learning and growth. We value potential, strong work ethic, and excellent written and verbal communication skills. Standout candidates demonstrate:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Excel, with an enthusiasm to develop more advanced skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good analytical and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in working with data and using it to solve business problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to communicate effectively with colleagues at all levels of the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive approach and willingness to learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A resilient, enthusiastic team player with strong self-motivation and a collaborative, hands-on approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in databases and data; previous exposure to SQL would be beneficial but is not essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in Business Intelligence and data visualisation; previous exposure to Power BI would be beneficial but is not essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in developing commercial and financial understanding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sense of fun&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applications close on &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Friday 30th October 2026 at 4.00pm.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whether you are joining a client facing team, a core services team, or starting out on your professional career journey, joining Brunswick unlocks a range of exceptional employee benefits to support your financial future, health and wellness, family and community and continuous professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h1&gt;About Brunswick&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brunswick is a global advisory firm. We help companies tackle high-stakes issues, navigate complex stakeholder relationships, and deliver high-impact outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our clients value our ability to anticipate, shape, and respond to the key players and forces in the financial and investment arena, regulatory and geopolitical universe, NGO community, workforce and beyond. They rely on us for deep experience, fresh perspectives and original thinking. So, in Brunswick you will find an exceptional range of experience and talent with a rich mix of backgrounds. From the beginning, we have prioritized attracting, developing, and retaining the best professionals in the industry, united by a culture of inclusivity, excellence, and intellectual curiosity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 1987 in London, the firm has organically grown to 27 offices in 18 countries across the Americas, Europe, Middle East, Africa, Asia and Australia. We operate as a “one-firm firm” with no individual profit centers. This allows us to assemble fully integrated, bespoke teams for each client, able to draw on the full resources of Brunswick anywhere in the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Brunswick is an equal opportunity employer. &amp;nbsp;All qualified applicants will be considered without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, disability, pregnancy, genetic information, or any other status protected by applicable law. Please&amp;nbsp;read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.brunswickgroup.com/app/uploads/Group-Privacy-Notice-for-Employees_April-2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Global Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; to understand how your data is managed.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
